{"seq":17,"slug":"neuropsychology","title":"神经心理学","stage":"DONE","category":"psychology","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/neuropsychology","rating":{"composite":3.71,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":4.2,"coverage":3.25,"positioning":4,"strategic":3.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":{"composite":3.21,"verdict":"neutral","uScore":2.5}},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"神经心理学-简介\">神经心理学 简介</h1><p>神经心理学研究脑与行为的关系——大脑结构和功能如何产生认知、情感与行为，以及脑损伤如何导致心理功能的可观测改变。它位于神经科学与心理学的交汇处，但有一个鲜明的方法论特征：<strong>以损伤-缺陷的双分离为推理工具，从行为表现反推认知架构与神经定位</strong>。本知识库的重心不在脑的分子细胞机制，而在&quot;脑区/网络损伤 → 认知缺陷模式 → 临床评估与康复&quot;这条从结构到行为再到干预的链条。</p>\n<h2 id=\"本-hub-与兄弟-hub-的分工边界\">本 hub 与兄弟 hub 的分工边界</h2><p>心理学下设多个与&quot;脑/认知&quot;相关的 hub，它们视角不同、各有侧重。下表帮助你判断某个问题应去哪里：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>你的问题</th>\n<th>应看的 hub</th>\n<th>与本 hub 的边界</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>神经元、突触、神经递质等分子细胞机制</td>\n<td>02 生物心理学</td>\n<td>本 hub 把这些当作前置知识，聚焦其行为后果</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>健康人的注意、记忆、语言如何运作（行为实验）</td>\n<td>03 认知心理学</td>\n<td>本 hub 关注这些功能&quot;损坏后&quot;暴露的组织结构</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>精神障碍的诊断、病因与心理治疗</td>\n<td>09 临床异常心理学</td>\n<td>本 hub 聚焦脑器质性损伤的认知后果，而非功能性精神障碍</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>感觉通道与知觉计算（视/听/多感觉）</td>\n<td>24 感觉与知觉</td>\n<td>本 hub 只在失认/忽略等&quot;知觉障碍&quot;处与之交接</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>测验的信度、效度、IRT、CAT 等测量学原理</td>\n<td>21 心理测量学</td>\n<td>本 hub 应用这些原理做临床评估，不展开测量理论本身</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>一句话区分：生物心理学问&quot;脑如何工作&quot;，认知心理学问&quot;心智如何工作&quot;，临床异常心理学问&quot;精神为何失常&quot;，而<strong>神经心理学问&quot;脑损伤后心智如何改变、如何测量、如何康复&quot;</strong>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"四章结构与推荐学习路径\">四章结构与推荐学习路径</h2><p>全书四章遵循&quot;基础 → 机制 → 评估 → 应用&quot;的递进：</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>脑与行为基础</strong>——功能神经解剖、脑可塑性、偏侧化与脑连接，建立结构-功能映射的坐标系。</li>\n<li><strong>认知神经心理学</strong>——注意与执行功能、记忆系统、语言与视空间加工，逐一拆解核心认知域的神经基础与障碍模式。</li>\n<li><strong>评估方法</strong>——神经心理测验、神经影像、生态化与数字评估，介绍把理论变成可测量证据的工具体系。</li>\n<li><strong>临床应用</strong>——神经退行性疾病、创伤性脑损伤、认知康复，将前三章整合为诊断与干预的实践。</li>\n</ol>\n<p>推荐路径按人群分流：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>初学者 / 跨学科入门</strong>：严格按 1→2→3→4 顺序通读。第一章是后续所有内容的解剖学地基，不可跳过。</li>\n<li><strong>已有认知心理学基础</strong>：可略读第一章解剖细节，重点放在第二章的&quot;障碍模式&quot;与第四章，体会损伤证据如何检验认知理论。</li>\n<li><strong>临床 / 康复方向</strong>：可先读第四章建立问题意识，再回到第二、三章补足机制与评估依据；第一章作为按需查阅的参考。</li>\n<li><strong>评估 / 测量方向</strong>：以第三章为主线，结合 21 心理测量学 hub 一起读。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"前置知识\">前置知识</h2><p>阅读本库最好已具备：基础的<strong>中枢神经系统解剖</strong>概念（脑叶、皮层下结构的大致分工）、<strong>认知心理学</strong>对注意/记忆/语言的基本术语，以及对<strong>标准化测验与常模</strong>的初步理解。缺乏这些背景的读者，建议先浏览 02 生物心理学的神经科学基础章与 03 认知心理学，再进入本库。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"brain-behavior-foundations","title":"脑与行为基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/neuropsychology/brain-behavior-foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"functional-neuroanatomy","title":"功能神经解剖学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/neuropsychology/brain-behavior-foundations/functional-neuroanatomy"},{"seq":2,"slug":"brain-plasticity-and-recovery","title":"脑可塑性与恢复","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/neuropsychology/brain-behavior-foundations/brain-plasticity-and-recovery"},{"seq":3,"slug":"lateralization-and-connectivity","title":"偏侧化与脑连接","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/neuropsychology/brain-behavior-foundations/lateralization-and-connectivity"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"cognitive-neuropsychology","title":"认知神经心理学","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/neuropsychology/cognitive-neuropsychology","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"attention-and-executive-functions","title":"注意与执行功能","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/neuropsychology/cognitive-neuropsychology/attention-and-executive-functions"},{"seq":2,"slug":"memory-systems-and-disorders","title":"记忆系统与障碍","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/neuropsychology/cognitive-neuropsychology/memory-systems-and-disorders"},{"seq":3,"slug":"language-and-visuospatial-processing","title":"语言与视空间加工","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/neuropsychology/cognitive-neuropsychology/language-and-visuospatial-processing"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"assessment-methods","title":"评估方法","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/neuropsychology/assessment-methods","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"neuropsychological-testing","title":"神经心理测验","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/neuropsychology/assessment-methods/neuropsychological-testing"},{"seq":2,"slug":"neuroimaging-techniques","title":"神经影像技术","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/neuropsychology/assessment-methods/neuroimaging-techniques"},{"seq":3,"slug":"ecological-and-digital-assessment","title":"生态化与数字评估","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/neuropsychology/assessment-methods/ecological-and-digital-assessment"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"clinical-applications","title":"临床应用","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/neuropsychology/clinical-applications","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"neurodegenerative-disorders","title":"神经退行性疾病","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/neuropsychology/clinical-applications/neurodegenerative-disorders"},{"seq":2,"slug":"traumatic-brain-injury","title":"创伤性脑损伤","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/neuropsychology/clinical-applications/traumatic-brain-injury"},{"seq":3,"slug":"cognitive-rehabilitation","title":"认知康复","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/neuropsychology/clinical-applications/cognitive-rehabilitation"}]}]}